  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1115 PM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nA quiet night of weather has settled in across the area with \ncalm winds and clear skies. The RAP's H5 jet analysis shows\nridging directly over eastern Nebraska/South Dakota. Deep closed\nlows spin off each coast. \n\nPrimary concern in the short-term is the probability of fog\ndevelopment overnight. Guidance is generally discouraging the\ninclusion of fog in the forecast, but the wind and dewpoint\ndepression suggest otherwise. Have limited fog to areas just \nsouth of the stationary front draped near the Platte River where\nmoisture is pooled and river valleys shielded from any wind. \nBelieve that the stronger winds just off the sfc should help \nlimit development. Confidence is low. Lows (and dewpoints) \nshould hit bottom in the low 50s under mostly clear skies.",
